class:: SpecCentroid2
summary:: Explicit spectral centroid in Hz
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/SpecCentroid

description::
Calculates the weighted mean frequency of a SuperCollider FFT frame. Bins from code::minFreq:: through code::maxFreq:: contribute either magnitude or power, and silence returns zero. The output updates when the FFT chain produces a new frame and otherwise retains that frame's result.

The implementation is a non-destructive reader of the FFT chain's spectral values. It is practically similar to link::Classes/SpecCentroid::, but makes spectrum convention, frequency limits, FFT size, units, and silence behavior explicit.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: chain
An FFT chain produced with the same literal size as code::fftSize::.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included frequency in Hz. Default 0 includes DC.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included frequency in Hz. Zero selects Nyquist.

argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 weights by magnitude; 1 weights by power.

argument:: fftSize
Literal FFT size: a power of two from 256 through 8192.

returns::
Centroid frequency in Hz, or 0 for silence.

instancemethods::

examples::
code::
(
Routine({
    var buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, buffer, BufRateScale.kr(buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        SpecCentroid2.kr(chain, fftSize: 1024).poll(5, "centroid Hz");
        (source * 0.15) ! 2
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::

